Run a 2-round A/B test to optimize the system prompt at src/dynamic_harness/core/agent_system_prompt.txt.

BE TERSE. Do not narrate plans or recap results. Verify minimally — if a delegate returns completed with non-empty artifacts, that's sufficient.

Use delegate(description, system_prompt=...) as the main tool. The system_prompt parameter overrides the sub-agent's default behavior. Each sub-agent gets full authority to decompose, delegate, and write files.

The directory .optimize_benchmarks/ already exists. pytest is NOT installed. Include "pytest NOT available, use python3 and assert statements" in any testing task.

# SEED PROMPT
Read the seed from src/dynamic_harness/core/agent_system_prompt.txt before generating variants.

# BENCHMARK TASKS
These are for evaluation only — do NOT solve them yourself.

## Task 1: File Discovery
  Description: "Find the 3 largest Python files in the current directory. Write the results (paths with sizes, sorted descending) to .optimize_benchmarks/largest_files.txt and report with that artifact. .optimize_benchmarks/ already exists."

## Task 2: Code Generation
  Description: "Write a Python function fibonacci(n) that returns the nth Fibonacci number using iteration (not recursion). Write assertion-based tests (not pytest) testing fibonacci(0)=0, fibonacci(1)=1, fibonacci(10)=55, fibonacci(20)=6765. Write to .optimize_benchmarks/fibonacci.py and .optimize_benchmarks/test_fibonacci.py. Run with python3 and confirm pass. pytest NOT available — use assert statements. .optimize_benchmarks/ exists."

## Task 3: Code Analysis
  Description: "Search the current directory recursively for TODO and FIXME comments in *.py, *.js, *.ts files. Write report to .optimize_benchmarks/todos.txt with format FILE:LINE: comment text, one per line. Report with that artifact. .optimize_benchmarks/ exists."

# INSTRUCTIONS

## Round 1: Baseline + 5 Variants

### Step 1: Read the seed prompt
  read("src/dynamic_harness/core/agent_system_prompt.txt")

### Step 2: Generate 5 variants
Delegate a sub-agent with the SEED TEXT embedded:
  "Generate 5 variant system prompts based on the seed below. Each variant should be roughly 1000-1800 characters. Be concise. Strip examples and redundant sections, but do NOT obsess over an exact character count — a correct, complete prompt is better than one truncated to hit a limit. Decide the length that best serves each focus; only re-work a variant if its content is actually broken or incomplete, not to chase an arbitrary target.

  Focus on: clarity of delegation rules, emphasis on writing to disk before reporting, better verification instructions.

  Variants:
  1. Speed/parallelism emphasis
  2. Thoroughness/verification emphasis
  3. Terse and directive-heavy
  4. Detailed and explanatory
  5. Token efficiency

  SEED PROMPT:
  [INSERT THE FULL SEED TEXT]

  Output ALL 5 variants as complete text labeled ### VARIANT N: name."

Write output to .optimize_benchmarks/variants.txt and verify it has 5 variants.

### Step 3: Test seed + 5 variants against 3 tasks (18 runs)
Test 6 prompts (seed + 5 variants) x 3 tasks = 18 runs.
- For SEED: delegate normally (no system_prompt override).
- For each VARIANT: delegate with system_prompt=[variant text].

Delegate in BATCHES of 6. Record for each: prompt, status, summary, artifact IDs.

### Step 4: Evaluate
Read artifacts. Evaluate each prompt on correctness, completeness, behavior.
Write .optimize_benchmarks/evaluation_round1.txt ranking all 6 prompts 1-6.

## Round 2: Refine Top 3

### Step 1: Generate 3 new variants
Delegate with top 3 texts embedded:
  "Generate 3 new variants by combining strengths of the 3 winning prompts below. Output complete texts labeled ### VARIANT N: name.

  WINNING PROMPT 1: [INSERT TEXT]
  WINNING PROMPT 2: [INSERT TEXT]
  WINNING PROMPT 3: [INSERT TEXT]"

### Step 2: Test 6 prompts (top 3 + 3 new) against 3 tasks (18 runs)
Delegate ALL 18 (prompt, task) pairs in batches of 6. Record results.

### Step 3: Evaluate
Write .optimize_benchmarks/evaluation_round2.txt ranking all 6 prompts.

## Final Report
Synthesize results. Report: best prompt (complete text), why it won, aggregate rankings, key insight.
Write best prompt to .optimize_benchmarks/best_prompt.txt.
Report with artifact_ids including all evaluation files and best_prompt.txt.